## Summary

Adds production-grade email verification for local password accounts while preserving federated identity semantics and existing users.

### Local account lifecycle
- V52 adds `users.email_verified_at` plus hash-only one-time email-verification credentials.
- Existing pre-V52 accounts are backfilled as verified to avoid unexpectedly locking out current users.
- New local-password registrations remain unverified when verification is required.
- Local password login is rejected before verification and cannot issue access/refresh sessions.
- Successful verification consumes the credential once and enables normal login.
- Resend returns the same generic accepted response for existing, verified and missing accounts.

### Federated identities
- Google/Apple accounts created from provider-verified email are marked verified immediately.
- An existing local account may become verified through the already-restricted authoritative Google linking path.
- Apple verification remains safe because the Apple token verifier rejects a supplied email claim when `email_verified` is false.

### Credential safety
- raw verification tokens are never persisted; PostgreSQL stores SHA-256 hashes only;
- issue/resend serialize on the user row and invalidate earlier active credentials;
- verify follows the same user-first lock order before locking the credential;
- expired tokens are durably invalidated;
- consumed tokens cannot be replayed;
- mail delivery happens asynchronously AFTER_COMMIT so SMTP latency/failure is outside the registration/resend transaction.

### Web UX
- registration routes unverified local accounts to `/verify-email` instead of attempting an impossible login;
- the verify page accepts token links and supports enumeration-safe resend with the registration email prefilled;
- provider-authenticated registrations continue directly into the authenticated app.

### Production contract
- production hard-wires `required=true` and SMTP delivery;
- required verification without SMTP fails configuration validation;
- production requires an HTTPS verification URL and explicit sender;
- production Compose forwards email verification TTL/retention/cleanup and SMTP configuration;
- `.env.example` keeps verification disabled locally by default.

### Validation added
- focused `EmailVerificationServiceTest` covers hash-only issuance, user-first locking, successful consumption, expiry invalidation, replay rejection and enumeration-safe resend;
- production Compose contract asserts mandatory verification configuration;
- dedicated `Email verification smoke` starts the real API with `required=true + smtp` and verifies registration gate, generic resend, hash-only persistence, one active credential, one-time verification, replay rejection and successful login after verification.

Exact PR head: `32aa9beb0b2a3e982ca1257fd9c6ae4a03aa2b66`.

## Merge gate

Do not merge until every PR-triggered workflow for the exact latest head SHA is green, the PR remains mergeable, and the branch is 0 behind `master`. Merge method must be a merge commit with an expected-head guard.
